{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment1.md","content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: register `disposeAll` via `addTearDown`, don't call it at the end of the body**

All five FAB-surface tests dispose their services as the **last statement** of the test body (lines 375, 409, 439, 473, 536). If any `expect` before it fails, `disposeAll` never runs and the `AgentService` idle watchdogs outlive the test — the exact leak the pre-existing test in this file warns about ("Shut down services so their idle watchdogs don't outlive the test") — and the failure surfaces later as confusing pending-timer noise in the shard instead of at the real assertion.

Tear-downs run even when the body throws:

```dart
final manager = FlutterSessionManager(env: env, sessionsRoot: '/sessions');
addTearDown(() => disposeAll(manager));
manager.addSession('original-session', _fakeService(env));
```

Then drop the trailing `disposeAll(manager);` from each body. Same one-line change at all five sites.
